  A1  sigma_r^2 = -sigma_t^2 in the deep field: the radial "dispersion" is NEGATIVE.
      A kinetic gas cannot have it. A medium with a shear modulus (a solid) can.
      Large-r closed form: sigma_t^2 = (1/2) sqrt(G M_b a0) = v_inf^2/2  (PD1 P7).

==============================================================================
B.  Can that anisotropic stress carry the lensing?
==============================================================================
  Active (Tolman) source of a static spherical configuration: rho + (p_r + 2 p_t)/c^2.
  Here p_r = Pi_rr, p_t = Pi_tt, and Pi_rr + Pi_tt = 0, so p_r + 2 p_t = Pi_tt.
  Fractional correction to the lensing source = (Pi_tt/c^2)/rho = sigma_t^2/c^2.
  Large-r closed form: sqrt(G M_b a0)/(2 c^2).

    log M_b    canonical          alt                what it must cover
       9     1.9611e-08        2.1559e-08         a factor 6 to 20 of halo mass
      10     6.2015e-08        6.8174e-08         a factor 6 to 20 of halo mass
      11     1.9611e-07        2.1559e-07         a factor 6 to 20 of halo mass
      12     6.2015e-07        6.8174e-07         a factor 6 to 20 of halo mass
      13     1.9611e-06        2.1559e-06         a factor 6 to 20 of halo mass
      14     6.2015e-06        6.8174e-06         a factor 6 to 20 of halo mass
      15     1.9611e-05        2.1559e-05         a factor 6 to 20 of halo mass

  B1  VERDICT: the anisotropic stress contributes ~1e-6 of the lensing source, against a
      shortfall of a factor 6 to 20. The stress tells you what the medium is; it does not
      pay the amount. The lensing signal is mass.

==============================================================================
C.  The amount budget
==============================================================================
  Budget: M_c <= 5.41 M_b (all the cold charge comoving with the galaxy's baryons).
  Law:    M_c(<r) = M_b X(x),  X(x) = (sqrt(1+4x^2)-1)/2,  x = r/r_M.
  X(x) = 5.41 at x = 5.8888 r_M. Beyond that the law's halo exceeds the entire
  cosmic cold budget, and X grows as x thereafter.

    log M_b    r_M [kpc]    budget gone at      at 30 r_M needs     ratio
  canonical:
       9           1.22          7.2 kpc          29.50 M_b        5.45x
      10           3.86         22.7 kpc          29.50 M_b        5.45x
      11          12.20         71.9 kpc          29.50 M_b        5.45x
      12          38.59        227.3 kpc          29.50 M_b        5.45x
  alt:
       9           1.11          6.5 kpc          29.50 M_b        5.45x
      10           3.51         20.7 kpc          29.50 M_b        5.45x
      11          11.10         65.4 kpc          29.50 M_b        5.45x
      12          35.11        206.7 kpc          29.50 M_b        5.45x

  C1  Required to pass KiDS host-free (ONE1): share X_s = 59.5 M_b.
      vs the 5.41 budget          : 11.00x over.
      vs the charge that falls in : 42x to 66x over (VSH1: 0.9-1.4 M_b).
  C2  T4 (exact: net polarization charge in any free-fall-bounded ball is 0 at all times,
      for any momentum equation) and LFS1 (exact: static polarization is frozen, the
      halo's charge changes only by O(|Phi|/c^2) ~ 1e-6) say the halo's charge EQUALS the
      dust charge carried in. So the cap is a conservation law, not a mechanism failure.
  C3  The one reconciliation: g_bar at KiDS radii is missing hot gas. The law would be
      evaluated with g_bar raised 11.0x there. The record's own note: "with B21's own
      hot-gas estimate in g_bar, its published outer points drop from 1.50 to 0.47 of the
      law. Nothing on disk measures that gas."

